misaki - https://github.com/hexgrad/misaki
Licensed under the Apache License, Version 2.0.

The grapheme-to-phoneme layer in src/g2p/ draws on misaki, Kokoro's own G2P:

  * src/g2p/en_us.tsv        is generated by tools/gen_en_data.py from
    src/g2p/en_gb.tsv        misaki's own us_gold.json/us_silver.json and
    src/g2p/en_us_verb.tsv   gb_gold.json/gb_silver.json pronunciation
    src/g2p/en_gb_verb.tsv   dictionaries (misaki/data/*.json) - words already
                             spelled in Kokoro's own phoneme alphabet. The
                             _verb.tsv files hold the subset of entries where
                             misaki's own data distinguishes a VERB-tagged
                             pronunciation from the default, used by the
                             verb-context heuristic in src/g2p/en.rs.
  * tools/gen_zh_data.py     ports the pinyin-to-IPA tables in
                             misaki/transcription.py, which generate
                             src/g2p/zh_syllables.rs.
  * src/g2p/zh.rs            follows the algorithm of ZHG2P.legacy_call in
                             misaki/zh.py.
  * tools/gen_ja_data.py     extracts the HEPBURN table from misaki/cutlet.py,
                             which generates src/g2p/ja_data.rs.
  * src/g2p/ja.rs            follows the algorithm of Cutlet._get_single_mapping
                             in misaki/cutlet.py.

src/g2p/en.rs (dictionary lookup, morphology and number expansion),
src/g2p/romance/ (Spanish/Italian/French/Brazilian Portuguese letter-to-sound
rules) and src/g2p/hi.rs (Devanagari letter-to-sound rules) are original,
from-scratch implementations, not ports of any misaki module.

